@identity = http://localhost:5081
@gateway = http://localhost:5080

### Sign in as the demo employee (through the gateway, as the SPA does)
### Sets the httpOnly refresh cookie; the access token is in the body.
# @name login
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@company.com",
  "password": "Demo@123"
}

### Capture the access token from the response above
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### The caller's own profile — no id in the URL
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Wrong password -> 401, with no hint that the account exists
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@company.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword1"
}

### Unknown email -> the same 401, and NO account is created
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "definitely-a-manager@example.com",
  "password": "AnyPassword1"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Two-factor authentication
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Current 2FA state for the caller
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/totp/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Begin enrolment -> returns the base32 secret and the otpauth:// URI for the QR code.
### 2FA is NOT on yet; the secret is inert until a code confirms it.
# @name totpSetup
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/totp/setup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Confirm enrolment with a live code -> returns the ten recovery codes, shown once.
### Also revokes every existing session, including this one.
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/totp/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "123456"
}

### Sign in again now that 2FA is on -> no access token, just an mfaToken
# @name mfaLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@company.com",
  "password": "Demo@123"
}

### Step two: the authenticator code (or a recovery code) completes the sign-in
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login/totp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mfaToken": "{{mfaLogin.response.body.mfaToken}}",
  "code": "123456"
}

### The mfaToken is issued for a different audience, so it is NOT an access token -> 401
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{mfaLogin.response.body.mfaToken}}

### Replace the recovery codes (invalidates any unused ones)
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/totp/recovery-codes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "123456"
}

### Turn 2FA off — needs the password as well as a code
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/totp/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "Demo@123",
  "code": "123456"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Sessions
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Exchange the refresh cookie for a new access token. The cookie rotates on every call;
### this is also how the SPA restores a session after a page reload.
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/refresh

### Run the line above TWICE without refreshing in between: the second call replays an
### already-rotated token, which is treated as theft and revokes the whole family.

### Sign out — revokes the family and clears the cookie
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Internal endpoints
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Via the gateway -> 404, blocked at the ingress
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/internal/users/8f7d3c1e-1b64-4a2f-9d05-6c1a7e93b420

### Direct, without the shared key -> 404
GET {{identity}}/api/auth/internal/users/8f7d3c1e-1b64-4a2f-9d05-6c1a7e93b420

### Direct, with the shared key -> 200
GET {{identity}}/api/auth/internal/users/8f7d3c1e-1b64-4a2f-9d05-6c1a7e93b420
X-Internal-Api-Key: {{$dotenv INTERNAL_API_KEY}}

### Health
GET {{identity}}/health
